{"version":3,"kind":"Article","sha256":"5f41e1f3bd551cf704e23feeb2e4c97a4a4e658b0860f797d4a91178635f3e72","slug":"future.fairmappings","location":"/future/FAIRMappings.md","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"Reusable Mappings as FAIR Resources","content_includes_title":false,"github":"https://github.com/Cross-Domain-Interoperability-Framework/cdifbook","numbering":{"title":{"offset":2}},"source_url":"https://github.com/Cross-Domain-Interoperability-Framework/cdifbook/blob/main/future/FAIRMappings.md","edit_url":"https://github.com/Cross-Domain-Interoperability-Framework/cdifbook/edit/main/future/FAIRMappings.md","exports":[{"format":"md","filename":"FAIRMappings.md","url":"/cdifbook/build/FAIRMappings-a798c2c21165034b71890822a2c442ab.md"}]},"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"It is recognized that transformations to both data and metadata at several levels are a critical part of data integration. The mappings used to inform transformations are a critical aspect of this, being both needed provenance information and also potentially providing a reusable FAIR resource in their own right. There is an RDA group working on ","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"h0NNrUBsJa"},{"type":"link","url":"https://mapping-commons.github.io/rda-fair-mappings/use-cases/","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"FAIR Mappings","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"CUDd9gQzFd"}],"urlSource":"https://mapping-commons.github.io/rda-fair-mappings/use-cases/","key":"iP3fGVRJfV"},{"type":"text","value":", and the CDIF WG follows this work and attempts to align with it. Currently, the use of A Simple Standard for Sharing Ontology mappings (","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"UeUHzUXZyv"},{"type":"link","url":"https://mapping-commons.github.io/sssom/dev/","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"SSSOM","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"RKghk6XZoA"}],"urlSource":"https://mapping-commons.github.io/sssom/dev/","key":"UD5EODOoFj"},{"type":"text","value":") is seen as a useful standard for the expression of mappings, with the RDF Mapping Language ","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"Cxfj7T0wz4"},{"type":"link","url":"https://rml.io/specs/rml/","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"RML","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"SN1WALmReF"}],"urlSource":"https://rml.io/specs/rml/","key":"LvD5ZYvQwj"},{"type":"text","value":" also proving to be of interest, This is an area where more work remains to be done, but will be the subject of a CDIF profile in the not-too-distant future.","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"D5foox7kHg"}],"key":"ZyEPC4pqPF"}],"key":"vWUgjkJCgK"}],"key":"lCjaUXfMoH"},"references":{"cite":{"order":[],"data":{}}},"footer":{"navigation":{"prev":{"title":"Standards for Data Description","url":"/data-description/dataintegrationstandards","group":"Open Topics, Future Profiles"},"next":{"title":"Provenance","url":"/future/provenance","group":"Open Topics, Future Profiles"}}},"domain":"http://localhost:3000"}